		{
			"id": "113873005628582502",
			"parentId": "113872931333209061",
			"url": "https://front-end.social/@eeeps/113873005592013867",
			"author": {
				"name": "Eric Portis",
				"url": "https://front-end.social/@eeeps",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/304/428/669/626/974/original/f87ff3e52bb789da.jpeg"
			},
			"date": "2025-01-22T16:42:52.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://front-end.social/@michelle\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>michelle</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://mastodon.social/@kornel\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>kornel</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://indieweb.social/@fershad\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>fershad</span></a></span> I discussed this article with <span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://mastodon.social/@jonsneyers\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>jonsneyers</span></a></span> when it was published. He pointed out that the energy used for network transfer from the server to the client should be accounted for; especially on mobile (radio), this costs much more than CPU decoding. He raised two other points:</p><p>- Energy used to light up the display &gt; both network and decode costs<br>- Encode costs, esp. for AVIF, dwarf decode costs. Worth thinking about # of loads.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "113873054013100042",
			"parentId": "113872931333209061",
			"url": "https://mastodon.social/@kornel/113873053828838898",
			"author": {
				"name": "Kornel",
				"url": "https://mastodon.social/@kornel",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/297/189/022/015/904/original/8e79f5a832580abb.jpg"
			},
			"date": "2025-01-22T16:55:08.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://front-end.social/@michelle\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>michelle</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://indieweb.social/@fershad\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>fershad</span></a></span> I don't think this should affect anyone's decision about use on regular web pages. The energy usage in absolute terms is too tiny to matter, even multiplied by millions it's still small.</p><p>But from overall energy efficiency perspective you should also consider that larger files will use relatively more energy on all the network equipment that sends them. </p><p>Computers and displays also use energy while waiting for a page to load. Faster pages reduce wasted time.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "113880045552979068",
			"parentId": "113873054013100042",
			"url": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat/113880045552979068",
			"author": {
				"name": "Zach Leatherman",
				"url": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/accounts/avatars/109/286/461/031/266/152/original/dc489c3746a44e00.png"
			},
			"date": "2025-01-23T22:33:13.522Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://mastodon.social/@kornel\" class=\"u-url mention\">@<span>kornel</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://front-end.social/@michelle\" class=\"u-url mention\">@<span>michelle</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://indieweb.social/@fershad\" class=\"u-url mention\">@<span>fershad</span></a></span> fwiw I went with your advice and I’m using `avif, auto` for now!</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "113883362835641882",
			"parentId": "113873054013100042",
			"url": "https://indieweb.social/@fershad/113883362808499212",
			"author": {
				"name": "fershad",
				"url": "https://indieweb.social/@fershad",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/367/590/565/962/969/original/cd716072029f969b.jpg"
			},
			"date": "2025-01-24T12:36:50.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://mastodon.social/@kornel\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>kornel</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://front-end.social/@michelle\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>michelle</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://front-end.social/@eeeps\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>eeeps</span></a></span>  thanks for this conversation. I understand the comments about the network energy, especially for radio networks, I didn't test that segment because:</p><p>1. There's no reliable means to measure it<br>2. Network energy is (as far as I know) pretty constant <a href=\"https://fershad.com/writing/website-carbon-beyond-data-transfer/#data-transfer-network-energy-usage\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" translate=\"no\" target=\"_blank\"><span class=\"invisible\">https://</span><span class=\"ellipsis\">fershad.com/writing/website-ca</span><span class=\"invisible\">rbon-beyond-data-transfer/#data-transfer-network-energy-usage</span></a></p><p>Eric's points on encoding are very valid, as is Kornel's point about efficiency. Both should be measured further in a more end-to-end kinda test scenario.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		}
	],
